# UST.G3DI H02 Split-Algebra Kernel Relations Theorem v1

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_H02_SPLIT_ALGEBRA_1274_KERNEL_RELATIONS`

G3DH proved that the selected H02 base-resolvent coupling has rank 4,748 at
all six roots of one completely split prime. G3DI replaces that rank-only
evidence with explicit relations.

## Exact finite kernel

At each root, exact sparse elimination selects the same 4,748 update columns
and the same 1,274 dependent columns. For each dependent coordinate `j`, G3DI
emits a normalized triangular relation

```text
e_j + sum_{i<j} n_ij e_i,
```

and reconstructs its complete 30,789-row bordered residual before accepting
it. All 1,274 residuals vanish at every root. Unit coefficients in distinct
dependent coordinates prove that these relations are independent.

The six root values interpolate uniquely to a degree-less-than-six matrix

```text
N_split(gamma),  shape 6022 x 1274,
```

over

```text
F_21817[gamma]/(m_gamma)
  = product of the six split field factors.
```

Evaluation of the interpolated matrix reproduces every root relation with
zero mismatch. Therefore

```text
Q_split N_split = 0,
rank(N_split) = 1274,
rank(Q_split) = 6022 - 1274 = 4748.
```

An independent verifier also selects sixteen relations across the full
range, solves their B89 core preimages with the separate exact chart solver,
and obtains zero `W A_core^-1 U N` residual.

## What Changed

The finite H02 defect is no longer a numerical rank observation. Its complete
dimension, normalization, selected/dependent coordinate partition and all
relation coefficients are explicit and hash-bound over the split algebra.

## Boundary

Reduction modulo one rational prime is not an automatic lift to
`Q(gamma)`. G3DI does not yet prove that the 1,274 relations survive in
characteristic zero, and therefore does not yet close
`rank_Q(gamma)(Q)=4748` or emit the second characteristic-zero Woodbury
factorization.

The sharp next theorem is a relation-lift theorem: compute the same normalized
relations at independent split primes, reconstruct candidates with a proved
bound, and verify the exact polynomial bordered identity over `Q(gamma)`.

No Archimedean H02 value, evolving source contraction, path integration,
integral marking, readout or `beta_C` decision is claimed.

